steps.description:
Define all TypeScript interfaces and types that form the project's domain backbone. These types encode the PRD's data model (Section 16) and prepare for investigation graph + RAG readiness.

Create `src/types/bundle.ts`:
- `BundleManifest`: { bundlePath, extractedPath, files: ArtifactEntry[], totalSize, extractedAt }
- `ArtifactEntry`: { relativePath, absolutePath, size, category: ArtifactCategory, mimeType? }
- `ArtifactCategory`: enum — 'analyzer', 'log', 'kubernetes-resource', 'event', 'config', 'cluster-info', 'helm-release', 'unknown'
- `BundleProfile`: { manifest, analyzerCount, logFileCount, resourceCount, eventCount, namespaces: string[], workloads: WorkloadSummary[], coverageGaps: string[], artifactsByCategory: Record<ArtifactCategory, number> }
- `WorkloadSummary`: { name, namespace, kind, replicas?, readyReplicas? }

Create `src/types/analyzer.ts`:
- `AnalyzerResult`: { name, title, message, severity: AnalyzerSeverity, iconKey?, iconUri?, isPass, isFail, isWarn, uri? }
- `AnalyzerSeverity`: 'error' | 'warn' | 'pass' | 'info'

Create `src/types/finding.ts` (per PRD Section 16):
- `Finding`: { id, title, severity: FindingSeverity, confidence: number (0-1), affectedComponents: string[], reasoningSummary, evidence: Evidence[], contradictionsChecked: string[], recommendedAction, missingEvidence: string[] }
- `Evidence`: { path, note, artifactType?: ArtifactCategory, timestamp? }
- `FindingSeverity`: 'critical' | 'high' | 'medium' | 'low' | 'info'

Create `src/types/kubernetes.ts`:
- `K8sResource`: { apiVersion, kind, metadata: K8sMeta, spec?: unknown, status?: unknown }
- `K8sMeta`: { name, namespace?, labels?, annotations?, creationTimestamp? }
- `PodStatus`: { phase, conditions: PodCondition[], containerStatuses: ContainerStatus[], restartCount }
- `PodCondition`: { type, status, reason?, message?, lastTransitionTime? }
- `ContainerStatus`: { name, ready, restartCount, state: ContainerState }
- `ContainerState`: { running?, waiting?: { reason, message? }, terminated?: { reason, exitCode, message? } }
- `K8sEvent`: { type, reason, message, involvedObject: { kind, name, namespace? }, firstTimestamp?, lastTimestamp?, count? }

Create `src/types/graph.ts` (investigation graph for AI graph system):
- `GraphNodeType`: 'finding' | 'evidence' | 'artifact' | 'hypothesis' | 'symptom'
- `GraphEdgeType`: 'supports' | 'contradicts' | 'causes' | 'correlates' | 'derived-from'
- `GraphNode<T>`: { id, type: GraphNodeType, data: T, metadata?: Record<string,unknown> }
- `GraphEdge`: { id, source, target, type: GraphEdgeType, weight?: number, note? }
- `InvestigationGraph`: { nodes: Map<string, GraphNode<unknown>>, edges: GraphEdge[] }
- `FindingTreeNode`: { finding: Finding, children: FindingTreeNode[], parent?: string } (for tree traversal)

Create `src/types/rag.ts` (RAG-readiness abstractions):
- `ChunkableArtifact`: { artifactId, path, content: string, category: ArtifactCategory }
- `Chunk`: { id, artifactId, content, startLine, endLine, metadata?: Record<string,unknown> }
- `RetrievalResult`: { chunk: Chunk, score: number }
- `RetrieverInterface`: { retrieve(query: string, topK: number): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> }

Create `src/types/index.ts` re-exporting all types.

Write basic type guard functions in `src/utils/type-guards.ts`:
- `isAnalyzerResult(x: unknown): x is AnalyzerResult`
- `isK8sResource(x: unknown): x is K8sResource`
- `isK8sEvent(x: unknown): x is K8sEvent`

Write unit tests in `src/utils/__tests__/type-guards.test.ts` verifying guards accept valid data and reject invalid data.
